The /dev/null Tournament was hard on thirteen this year.
She took a beating even in every viable game, and things
started to take off around 11/26.  I had never ascended in
less than 3 weeks before that, and pulled out all of the
stops to try and finish a game before the end of November. 
I managed to get the Amulet halfway out of Gehennom when I
ran out of charges in my wand of death.  Paranoid the Wizard
would take me down and playing faster than I ever had
before, I opted to pick up a cockatrice corpse midway
through Asmodeus' level.  An overly zealous commitment to
Bushido had prevented me from taking out any peaceful
tengus, and switching between the ring of teleport control
and the ring of levitation eventually caught up with me.  I
walked right into a pit and turned to stone an hour and a
half after midnight on 12/1.  To make matters worse,
/dev/null has cracked down on end times.  Though I had the
Amulet when I died, the game wasn't scored because it ended
after 11/30, so I came out of the tournament with the
Plastic Star, the furthest any of my other games this year
had reached.  

Regardless, after finally learning the early game ropes, I
knew I had the chops to finish my first Samurai ascension.

The concept for Thirteen was formed one day when some
friends were telling me about a friend of theirs, a girl
named Thirteen who defended herself using detached scisor
blades.  Immeditely I though of daisho, and my first viewing
of "Seven Samurai" when I was young.  In the scene where
Kikuchiyo presents the stolen credentials of a young samurai
in order to join Kambei's crew, the subtitle translation I
watched at the time saw Heihachi mock the drunken Kikuchio,
exhorting "courage, thirteen!" refering to the age of the
credentials' owner. 

In order to customize things a bit, thirteen's little dog
was named "Rikichi", her fruit was "rice ball" (it was that
or millet, and millet sounded kind of gross), and when
applicable, her horse was "Yohei's horse".

After the tournament was over I was committed.  The only
public server where the name "thirteen" wasn't already taken
was hack.eotl.org, which sadly does not seem to maintain a
working high score list, so unfortunalty USENET will be the
only record of thirteen's legacy.

An armory granted thirteen her first boon.  Speed boots and
a cloak of protection were available for cheap, and made the
crucial difference in the early game.  Despite a few
setbacks (a throne dropping her charisma to 3, and a nearly
endless series of polymorph traps - plains centaur, lemure,
guardian naga, iguana, 2 new women, one of which dropped her
2 experience levels, a tiger, and iron piercer), the
discovery of dwarvish mithril and the Christmas reward of an
amulet of reflection in Sokoban laid further groundwork for
a successful venture.

Another throne granted thirteen the ability to see
invisible, and the discovery of plot's bones at the occupied
altar in gnometown gave her a stethoscope and an ample
supply of cursed potions for holy water.  Plot was killed by
a white unicorn, who remained hostile afterward, even to
Lawful individuals.  I didn't know that happened, so there
was some loss of luck after dealing with that perpetrator.
Worse, an accidental use of the 'y' key resulted in an
attack on the altar's attending priest, so the mines had to
be vacated for a time.

Back in the Dungeons of Doom, things started to look up,
starting with cold resistance from a winter wolf corpse and
a free genocide from a throne (bye bye Arch-Liches!).  The
first altar wasn't until level 9, but they showed up
regularly after that down to 19.  A leprechaun, Elvenking,
and series of stalkers on the Quest provided teleportitis,
sleep resistance, and invisibility, respectively.

The Quest was relatively straighforward once invisible, and
the bevy of wands of sleep made Ashikaga Takauji a snap.  It
took effort to hold back with the Tsurugi, which for the
last two years has conferred such bloodlust on thirteen that
it has been all but impossible to survive through the mid
game.  The appearance of a mind flayer instituted caution,
though, as even the single brain sucking was maddening.
Continuing with the mixed messaging from the RNG was the
appearance of a hostile tengu which upon consumption resulted
in...poison resistance :O  Later, some rather distracted 
ncubus dialiances resulted in a vampire taking advantage of
some casual nudity, resulting in the loss of 3 experience
levels.

Fortunately things picked up after that.  A fire ant
provided fire resistance, and some very un-bushidolike
conduct following between the failed tournament ascension
and the whole "poison resistance" fiasco resulted in some
tengu rage.  Teleport control attained.  A return visit to
plot's bones now that thirteen could survive an angry prist
resulted in the discovery of a cloak of magic resistance,
permanently ending the scourge of polymorph traps.

It was time to take on Medusa, but there was a problem.  No
water walking boots or levitation on demand had made itself
available by this point, and thirteen had only discovered a
single wand of cold.  Some holy water production and
blessing of a couple of charging scrolls got her to Medusa's
island.  Thanks to Sokoban's amulet, Medusa was not an
issue. and the previous discovery of a tinning kit ensured
preservation of black dragon meat while cleaning out the
castle, facilitated by the dicovery a pair of cursed
levitation boots dipped in holy water.  A pair of Gauntlets
of Power in the castle armory didn't hurt either.  The
castle liches were dealt with by enticing them to fall down
holes with the intent to genocide them later.

Enter the wand, and the first wishes thirteen obtained
access to during her travels.  She already had a spare
blessed scroll of charging after the pre-Medusa alchemy, so
every available charge went to a situationally appropriate
wish.  The blessed Orb of Detection ensured the persistence
of magic resistance through the end of the game and what I
hope to be my final flirtation with Artifact wishing.  A
wish for 2 blessed scrolls of genocide yielded only one, but
that was enough to ensure that liches never darkened
thirteen's horizons again.  A blessed fireproof bag of
holding ensured that her encumbrance issues would finally be
manageable, and a blessed ring of levitation ensured that
the -1 boots of levitation no longer need be relied upon.
At this point the wand was empty, and thirteen opted to hold
it rather than wrest immediately.

The Valley of the Dead yielded a spellbook of identify,
which became useful later.  The Tsurugi made short work of
Jubilex.  Another bout of alchemy resulted in the discovery
of a ring of conflict, a helm of brilliance, and holy water
enabling the blessing of another scroll of genocide, which
was lovingly directed at 'h' in order to deal with the mind
flayer community and whomever else.

Asomdeus and Baalzebub neatly dispatched, it was time to
make more holy water and get started on weapon collection.
Excalibur was recovered eventually while #dip'ing cursed
potions lifted from plot's bones.  Snickersnee was granted
almost immediately, followed by Frost Brand.  After that
Vlad wasn't even a challenge.  Upon claiming the amulet it
was time to wrest the final wish, and blessed greased +2
silver dragon scale mail was achieved.  Orcus and Yeenoghu
were handily dispatched.

On a final trek for holy water, thirteen accidentally
sacrificed a nurse, probably the piece that prevented her
from obtaining any other interesting artifact weapons,
though by this time it just made sense to create Orcrist and
Sting.  Her last wish, gleaned from a found (and later
blessed) magic lamp, was for a blessed ring of free action.
Extended nurse dancing and alchemy resulted in over 500 HP,
and an eventual AC of -17.  It was finally time to begin the
ascension run.

Orcus' wand of death made short work of the Wizard, and
subsequently discovered wands ensured his resurrections all
met the same fate, as did the more troublesome defenders of
Moloch's sanctum.  The escape from Gehennom was much less
problematic than the maddening attempt during the
tournament.  The journey upstairs and through the planes was
straightforward, though thirteen failed to pick up the bag
of gold and gems stashed on level 4.  The Orb of Detection
made the portals easy to find.  

The Astral Plane was tedious.  By the time thirteen had
established her endgame outfit, Pestilence was already too
close for comfort.  She headed toward Death, taking him out
with magic missile, +5 Front Brand and +6 Katana.  A wayward
magic missle made the first altar attendant (Raijin) a tad
upset.  Interspersed zaps from wants of death or teleport
ensured thirteen's transition from there to Susanowo's
altar, than finally to that of Amaterasu Omikami...


